    "id": "tender_496719/1531122",
    "title": "Cyber Secuirty Design Authority",
    "description": "Cyber Security Design Authority (CSDA)\r\n\r\n1. The Contracting Authority for this requirement is Strategic Command (UKStratCom) which\r\nis part of the Ministry of Defence (MoD). UKStratCom supports the MoD by making sure that joint\r\ncapabilities such as medical services, training and education, intelligence and information systems\r\nare developed and managed across all five of the land, sea, air, space and cyber domains. The\r\nAuthority also manages overseas joint operations.\r\n2. The Cyber Resilience Programme sits within the Crypto & Defensive Cyber delivery team\r\nwithin Defence Digital which itself is part of UKStratCom. The CSDA Close Support Partner will be\r\nfunded by, and accountable to both the Cyber Resilience Programme and the Defence Digital\r\nCyber Security Architecture team.\r\n3. The Defence Digital Cyber Security Architecture team sits within the 2-star Directorate of\r\nCyber Defence & Risk. It is part of the 1-star Cyber Strategy & Architecture function. The CSA team\r\nwork alongside Cyber Strategy & Innovation and the Defensive Cyber Joint User.\r\n\r\nThe Cyber Security Design Authority (CSDA) will be responsible for the design, creation,\r\nand improvement of security architecture products in support of Defence Digital strategy\r\nand the associated delivery plans, and in accordance with the established delivery method\r\nused within Defence Digital.",
